# Test fixtures are compared byte-for-byte by the suites that embed or load
# them. Without a rule here, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows CI
# runner uses that default) rewrites their line endings to CRLF and every such
# comparison fails there while passing on machines that check out LF. Pin them
# to LF everywhere, and mark the opaque formats as binary so no filter touches
# them at all.
crates/format/tests/fixtures/*.json text eol=lf
crates/photrez/tests/fixtures/*.json text eol=lf
crates/photrez/tests/baseline/manifest.json text eol=lf
crates/photrez/assets/i18n/*.json text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ttf binary
*.ptz binary
*.rgba binary
